A1_src: SRC := /opt/data/workspace/hermes-context/ (host-mount canonical)
A1_dst: DST := /workspace/hermes-context/ (exists: INDEX.md, agents/, config/)
A2_dir: sync one-way host -> workspace; ∀ op -> ¬write(SRC)
A3_standalone: script works sans systemd; units are user-level (systemctl --user), no root
A4_fallback: ¬rsync -> cp -a/tar-pipe path; sync CONTENTS src/ -> dst, ¬nest
A5_mirror: ∀ path -> DST end state == SRC end state, recursive; stale DELETED both paths
A6_dryrun: --dry-run -> ∀ writes = ∅ incl. logs; DST byte-identical pre/post
A7_recursive: cp-path reconciliation deletes stale subtrees ∀ depth
A8_placement: log always outside DST (~/.cache default); install paths outside mirrored tree (~/.local/bin); sync never deletes own entrypoints
A9_class: mirror equivalence = {contents, dir structure recursive, symlinks}; ∉ {metadata, timestamps, hardlink topology}; verify FAIL nonzero on mismatch, ¬warn-exit-0
A10_severity: FAIL only normal-op defects; exotic -> KNOWN_LIMITATIONS in +open, non-blocking
A11_guard: guard(SRC==DST) mandatory; ¬rm -rf DST before verified copy of SRC elsewhere
A12_identity: compare realpath(SRC) vs realpath(DST); refuse clean-nonzero-no-writes on equal/ancestor/descendant/symlink-into-SRC; both paths, pre-destructive
open: KNOWN_LIMITATIONS (A10-class, non-blocking)
invariants: [A2_dir, A5_mirror, A6_dryrun, A8_placement, A11_guard, A12_identity]
